AWS-014 — Workflow Monitoring

Document ID: AWS-014
Title: Workflow Monitoring
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Monitoring Model (CWMM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Monitoring Model establishes the principles, architecture, telemetry mechanisms, health assessment, performance observation, event monitoring, and operational visibility required to continuously observe Workflow Definitions, Workflow Instances, Workflow Programs, and execution environments while preserving determinism, governance, and engineering integrity.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Monitoring architecture
Runtime observation
Telemetry
Performance monitoring
Health assessment
Alerts
Dashboards
Operational visibility

This specification applies to every active Workflow Instance and Workflow Program.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Monitoring is the governed observation and measurement of workflow execution, operational health, and execution performance without modifying workflow semantics or execution behavior.

Monitoring observes execution.

It SHALL NOT alter execution.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Monitoring Model SHALL:

Provide operational visibility.
Detect abnormal behavior.
Measure workflow performance.
Support governance.
Enable operational response.
Preserve execution integrity.
Support continuous improvement.
Maintain traceability.
5. Monitoring Principles

Every workflow monitoring implementation SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Non-Intrusive Observation

Monitoring SHALL NOT influence workflow execution.

Continuous Visibility

Active workflows SHALL remain observable throughout execution.

Explainability

Monitoring results SHALL identify:

Observed workflow.
Observed activity.
Observation timestamp.
Observation rationale.
Supporting evidence.
Traceability

Every observation SHALL remain permanently attributable.

Timeliness

Monitoring SHALL provide information suitable for operational decision-making.

Governance

Monitoring SHALL comply with applicable Canonical Policy Objects.

